      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Watering: Clemson says water when the medium feels dry and never dry out completely; NC State says keep moist but fast-draining. Mapped to let_top_dry. Light: Clemson light shade, NC State partial shade with bright winter light; mapped to bright_indirect. Temperature 70 to 80 F (both) is the growing-season range; buds set at cooler nights (Clemson 50 to 68 F, NC State a run of nights near 40 F). Size: NC State 9 to 12 in tall, 1 to 2 ft wide. The ASPCA page read is for Schlumbergera bridgesii (Christmas or Easter cactus), a different species, so toxicity is genus-level. Humidity and growth rate: no number or statement."
      },
